        "t": 624.6611068359376,
        "r": 291.38770000000034,
        "b": 602.1032492035389
      },
      "content": "Connect a voltage source to one side of relay contacts.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_293",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_4",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_4",
          "title": "4. Engine Control Service"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_293",
          "title": "HEATER (GLOW PLUG) RELAY CHECK (K13)"
        }
      ],
      "page": 22,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0287",
      "reading_order": 296,
      "section": "HEATER (GLOW PLUG) RELAY CHECK (K13)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 55.842500000000015,
        "t": 586.7342068359377,
        "r": 291.5989000000003,
        "b": 526.249449203539
      },
      "content": "Connect a voltmeter to other side of relay contact  and  voltage  source.    If  voltage  appears when relay energizes, the contact is good.  The voltage reading appears in reverse order when checking normally closed (NC) contacts.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_293",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_4",
      "section_level": 2,
