    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0290",
      "reading_order": 299,
      "section": "FUEL SOLENOID CHECK (K14)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.5654,
        "t": 461.8381068359375,
        "r": 291.72029999999995,
        "b": 439.2230492035387
      },
      "content": "If there is fuel to the injection pump, but no fuel at the injection nozzle, the fuel solenoid may be defective.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_298",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_4",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_4",
          "title": "4. Engine Control Service"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_298",
          "title": "FUEL SOLENOID CHECK (K14)"
        }
      ],
      "page": 22,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0291",
      "reading_order": 300,
      "section": "FUEL SOLENOID CHECK (K14)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.56650000000001,
        "t": 423.9101068359375,
        "r": 291.56630000000047,
        "b": 363.4253492035388
      },
      "content": "To check solenoid operation, watch for solenoid actuation when B+ is applied (start switch in start or run position).  If there is no actuation when B+ is applied, the fuel solenoid must be replaced.  When B+ is removed, the solenoid must de-activate.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_298",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_4",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_4",
          "title": "4. Engine Control Service"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_298",
          "title": "FUEL SOLENOID CHECK (K14)"
        }
      ],
      "page": 22,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
