    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0300",
      "reading_order": 309,
      "section": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9386,
        "t": 584.5783068359375,
        "r": 564.8163000000002,
        "b": 562.0204492035388
      },
      "content": "Make certain that the generator set starting battery is good before beginning this check.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_308",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_4",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_4",
          "title": "4. Engine Control Service"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_308",
          "title": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)"
        }
      ],
      "page": 22,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0301",
      "reading_order": 310,
      "section": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2161,
        "t": 549.2023068359375,
        "r": 565.0835999999999,
        "b": 514.0021492035388
      },
      "content": "Unplug CB12-2A from the circuit breaker.  Note the markings on the wire to select the correct one.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_308",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_4",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_4",
          "title": "4. Engine Control Service"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_308",
          "title": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)"
        }
      ],
      "page": 22,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0302",
      "reading_order": 311,
      "section": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2150000000001,
        "t": 501.18400683593757,
        "r": 564.9835000000003,
        "b": 465.98384920353885
      },
      "content": "Locate S6 (oil pressure switch) on the generator set (see Figure 2-2).  Find the grounded side of S6, using a continuity tester.",
      "hyperlink_hint": true,
      "section_id": "sec_auto_308",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_4",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_4",
          "title": "4. Engine Control Service"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_308",
          "title": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)"
        }
      ],
      "page": 22,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0303",
      "reading_order": 312,
      "section": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2139000000001,
        "t": 453.1657068359376,
        "r": 564.8790000000002,
        "b": 430.6078492035389
      },
      "content": "Use a jumper to ground the non-grounded side of S6.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_308",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_4",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_4",
          "title": "4. Engine Control Service"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_308",
          "title": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)"
        }
      ],
      "page": 22,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0304",
      "reading_order": 313,
      "section": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2128000000001,
        "t": 417.78970683593764,
        "r": 564.7810999999999,
        "b": 369.94724920353895
      },
      "content": "Use a second jumper from the B+ terminal on the  control  board to apply B+ to the SW B+ (switched B+) terminal.  Fuel pump E5 should start and run.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_308",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_4",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_4",
          "title": "4. Engine Control Service"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_308",
          "title": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)"
        }
      ],
      "page": 22,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0305",
      "reading_order": 314,
      "section": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2128000000001,
        "t": 357.1291068359377,
        "r": 564.9537999999993,
        "b": 309.229449203539
      },
      "content": "Remove the B+ jumper.  If the fuel pump continues to run, K12 is good.  If the fuel pump stops, K12  has  failed  and  the  A11  control  board should be replaced.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_308",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_4",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_4",
          "title": "4. Engine Control Service"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_308",
          "title": "POWER RELAY CHECK (A11-K12)"
        }
      ],
      "page": 22,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
